---
import Callout from "@/components/Callout.astro";
import DocsLayout from "@/layouts/DocsLayout.astro";

const engagementContents = [
  [
    "Context",
    "The platform resource or experience this engagement belongs to.",
  ],
  [
    "Role",
    "The identity and responsibilities the platform assigns within that context.",
  ],
  [
    "Delegation",
    "The signed maximum and user-narrowed permissions available to the role.",
  ],
  [
    "Capabilities",
    "Versioned semantics mapped to concrete platform MCP tools.",
  ],
  [
    "Skills",
    "Signed declarative guidance compatible with the role and capabilities.",
  ],
  ["Lifetime", "Issued-at, expiration, renewal, revocation, and audit state."],
];

const isolationRules = [
  "Every invocation names exactly one engagement.",
  "Capability and tool maps are maintained independently.",
  "Credentials or derived tokens cannot be silently reused across contexts.",
  "Skill versions and caches remain scoped to the engagement.",
  "Platform data keeps its handling labels when used locally.",
  "Ambiguous intent requires the person or platform to disambiguate.",
];
---

<DocsLayout
  pageId="engagements"
  title="Registrations and Engagements"
  description="How BYOAg separates durable platform registrations from temporary, isolated engagements."
>
  <section class="bg-[#07111f] py-20">
    <div class="page-shell max-w-4xl">
      <p class="eyebrow">Relationship and operating context</p>
      <h1 class="mt-4 text-5xl font-black leading-tight text-paper">
        Register once. Engage in bounded contexts.
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-6 max-w-3xl text-xl leading-8 text-paper/74">
        A registration is the durable relationship between an agent installation
        and a platform account. An engagement is one temporary, isolated context
        in which that relationship can act.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-[#0b1626] py-20">
    <div class="page-shell">
      <div class="grid gap-4 lg:grid-cols-[0.8fr_auto_1.2fr] lg:items-stretch">
        <article
          class="rounded-lg border border-accent/40 bg-accent/[0.07] p-6"
        >
          <p class="eyebrow">Durable</p>
          <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-black text-paper">
            Platform registration
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-4 leading-7 text-paper/70">
            Links the human account, pairwise agent identity, local
            installation, registration policy, and key-bound credential.
          </p>
        </article>
        <div
          class="hidden items-center text-3xl font-light text-cyan lg:flex"
          aria-hidden="true"
        >
          →
        </div>
        <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
          <article class="rounded-lg border border-cyan/35 bg-cyan/[0.06] p-5">
            <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase text-cyan">Engagement A</p>
            <h3 class="mt-3 text-xl font-bold text-paper">Match 1 · Player</h3>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-paper/64">
              Its own grant, capabilities, skills, data policy, expiration, and
              audit trail.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article
            class="rounded-lg border border-white/14 bg-white/[0.04] p-5"
          >
            <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase text-paper/52">
              Engagement B
            </p>
            <h3 class="mt-3 text-xl font-bold text-paper">Match 2 · Player</h3>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-paper/64">
              Simultaneously active but independently validated and authorized.
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-6 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-6 text-paper/52">
        The two matches mirror the current reference-host fixture. They
        demonstrate isolation; they are not a universal game model.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-paper py-20 text-ink">
    <div class="page-shell grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-2">
      <article>
        <p class="eyebrow">Registration</p>
        <h2 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-black">
          A local reference, not a global identity
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-8 text-ink/70">
          The connector returns its own local registration UUID to the agent.
          The platform’s registration identifier stays inside the protocol
          implementation and is never treated as globally meaningful.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 leading-7 text-ink/70">
          Public registration results can show the platform, agent display name,
          status, creation time, and credential expiration. Tokens and private
          keys remain in the connector vault.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="rounded-lg border border-ink/12 bg-[#fff8ed] p-6 sm:p-8">
        <p class="eyebrow">Device continuity</p>
        <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-black">
          Agent identity is not session recovery
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-5 leading-7 text-ink/70">
          A new device creates a new installation key. The platform decides
          whether to treat it as a replacement, key rotation, or a separate
          registration. Reusing an agent’s display identity does not
          automatically migrate its conversations, memories, or credentials.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-[#07111f] py-20">
    <div class="page-shell">
      <div class="max-w-3xl">
        <p class="eyebrow">Signed engagement descriptor</p>
        <h2 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-black text-paper">
          Everything needed to evaluate one context
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-8 text-paper/70">
          Before activation, the connector validates the descriptor’s schema,
          issuer, signature, registration binding, delegation, and lifetime.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="mt-10 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
        {
          engagementContents.map(([title, text]) => (
            <article class="rounded-lg border border-white/12 bg-white/[0.04] p-5">
              <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-paper">{title}</h3>
              <p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-paper/66">{text}</p>
            </article>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-paper py-20 text-ink">
    <div class="page-shell grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[0.8fr_1.2fr]">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Concurrent engagements</p>
        <h2 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-black leading-tight">
          Isolation is explicit, not inferred
        </h2>
      </div>
      <ul class="grid gap-3" role="list">
        {
          isolationRules.map((rule) => (
            <li class="flex gap-3 rounded-md border border-ink/12 bg-white p-4 leading-7 text-ink/72">
              <>
                <span class="font-bold text-cyan" aria-hidden="true">
                  •
                </span>
                <span>{rule}</span>
              </>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-[#0b1626] py-20">
    <div class="page-shell grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-2">
      <article>
        <p class="eyebrow">Renewal and reduction</p>
        <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-black text-paper">
          Authority can shrink immediately
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-8 text-paper/70">
          Engagement lifetimes are platform-defined. Renewal is allowed only
          while the registration and delegation remain valid. Permission
          reduction takes effect immediately; expansion requires renewed user
          consent.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <p class="eyebrow">Revocation and disconnect</p>
        <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-black text-paper">
          Removal stays scoped
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-8 text-paper/70">
          A revoked engagement fails closed and loses its overlay. Disconnecting
          a registration asks the platform to revoke it before deleting its
          local credentials and state. Unrelated registrations and non-BYOAg
          agent files remain untouched.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-[#07111f] py-20">
    <div class="page-shell max-w-4xl">
      <Callout title="Current implementation boundary">
        The connector currently lists registrations and retrieves,
        schema-validates, and signature-verifies concurrent engagements. The
        reference host returns two isolated in-memory examples. Platform-driven
        engagement creation, renewal, derived tokens, tool routing, and
        data-label enforcement remain further work.
      </Callout>
      <a
        class="mt-8 inline-flex rounded-md border border-white/18 px-5 py-3 font-bold text-paper transition hover:border-cyan hover:bg-white/[0.06]"
        href="/protocol/capabilities"
      >
        Continue to permissions and capabilities
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</DocsLayout>
